    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A federation created in 1887 joining Cochinchina, Annam, Tonkin and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#cambodia">Cambodia</a>, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#laos">Laos</a> added after 1893.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rice">Rice</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#rubber">rubber</a> and state monopolies on opium, salt and alcohol made it <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a>’s most valuable Asian possession.</li><li>Japanese occupation and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#first-indochina-war">the First Indochina War</a> ended French rule at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Dien Bien Phu</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#geneva">Geneva</a> in 1954.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#paul-doumer">Paul Doumer</a>, who built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#indochina">Indochina</a>’s federal government and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hanoi">Hanoi</a> bridge first named after him, later became President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a> and was assassinated in 1932.</p></aside>
    </section>

