nter northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#indochina">Indochina</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#france">France</a>’s defeat</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1945</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#japan">Japan</a> overthrows French rule; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a> proclaims the Democratic Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#vietnam">Vietnam</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1946</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#first-indochina-war">The First Indochina War</a> begins after fighting in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#haiphong">Haiphong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#hanoi">Hanoi</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1954</span><span class="rf-text">Defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Dien Bien Phu</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#geneva-accords-1954">Geneva Accords</a> end <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#indochina">French Indochina</a></span></li></ol>
